+- CLI command `frai eval` wrapping the core harness, with optional `--threshold` gates for CI/CD.
 
 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Gating for CI/CD
+- CLI supports `--threshold <metric>=<min>` (repeatable) to fail the command if any metric falls below a minimum.
+- Exit code 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any threshold fails, 2 if a threshold is malformed or references an unknown metric.
+- Reports (JSON and Markdown) include a `thresholds` list (or section) showing pass/fail status for each threshold.
+- A metric with no score (e.g., exact match without references) fails its threshold.
+- SDK users can pass `thresholds` array to `generateReport` to get the same behavior programmatically.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
+- Custom metrics work with thresholds as long as they include an `id` and `score` field.
 
